full suite with bin/rails test"],"summary":"The environment is ready: Ruby 4.0.0 from Homebrew, gems in vendor/bundle, PostgreSQL 14 running as a brew service, and the test DB created and migrated. The first full run gave 6334 runs, 34637 assertions, 20 failures, 1 error and 25 skips, and took about 8 minutes. 13 of those 21 problems came from this Mac. 12 were wiki ordering tests, caused by the macOS en_US.UTF-8 collation, and I fixed them by recreating the DB with C collation. 1 was the Gantt PNG export error, caused by ImageMagick having no default font, and I fixed it with minimagick_font_path. Rerunning the affected files (213 tests) gave 0 failures. A second full run started but had not finished when I had to report, so the final total is not confirmed. I expect 8 failures to remain. They are not caused by this environment, and I did not change any code or tests for them. (1) 7 asset-link tests fail: LayoutTest#test_wiki_formatter_header_tags, ThemesTest x3, and IssuesControllerTest x3 (svg icon href). They use assert_select with a :match regex that contains `\\w`. rails-dom-testing 2.3.0 puts the regex inside a CSS string, and the Nokogiri 1.19.6 CSS parser drops the backslash, so `\\w` becomes `w`. I checked this on a minimal document: a regex with `\\w` fails and `[0-9a-f]+` passes, even though the rendered hrefs are correct. (2) CommonMark::SanitizationFilterTest#test_should_sanitize_html_strings expects `>` and `<` without escaping inside an attribute, but the current sanitize/nokogiri escapes them. Both look like changes in newer gem versions picked up by a fresh bundle install (there is no committed Gemfile.lock). 25 tests skip, including Bazaar and CVS because bzr and cvs are not installed. PostgreSQL must stay running for the test command to work.","human_needed":["The 7 assert_select `:match(..., /...\\w+.../)` failures and the CommonMark sanitization failure seem to come from the current gem versions (nokogiri 1.19.6, rails-dom-testing 2.3.0, sanitize 7.0.1), since there is no committed Gemfile.lock. Are they known upstream, or should a specific nokogiri version be pinned (for example in Gemfile.local) for local runs?","Should the Bazaar and CVS SCM tests also run locally? That needs bzr (breezy) and cvs installed, and ci:setup rerun with them added to SCMS.","vendor/bundle is not in .gitignore, so it shows as untracked. Is that OK, or should gems be installed outside the repo?"]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":203,"cache_read_input_tokens":69003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":203},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25389735-d0e0-48c8-836b-ea4afb0b9a85","uuid":"93158826-3614-4cb2-97c2-1a3b1326e635","timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:20:21.712Z","request_id":"req_011Cgdmu8C9S5hH6HQ9DAbr5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012M6wzz3k5Bxz2kmJBPzwc1":{"status":"done","test_command":"PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/ruby/bin:$PATH bin/rails test","setup_steps":["Read .github/workflows/tests.yml and .github/actions/setup-redmine/action.yml. CI runs `bin/rails test` with Ruby 3.3/3.4/4.0 on PostgreSQL 14, MySQL 8.4 or SQLite3. The system Ruby is 2.6, which is too old (Gemfile needs >= 3.3).","Used Homebrew Ruby 4.0.0 (/opt/homebrew/opt/ruby/bin, already installed; 4.0 is in the CI matrix) and Homebrew postgresql@14 (already installed; same major version as CI).","brew services start postgresql@14","psql -d postgres -c \"CREATE ROLE redmine LOGIN SUPERUSER PASSWORD 'redmine';\"","Wrote config/database.yml (gitignored) with only a test section: adapter postgresql, database redmine_test, username redmine, password redmine, host 127.0.0.1, template template0, collation C, ctype en_US.UTF-8. The C collation is