{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdoRQwfY9tAD69XVR4fW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`/tmp/redmine_test.log` holds the first run, from before I fixed the environment: 6334 runs, 34637 assertions, 20 failures, 1 error, 25 skips.\n\nThat result is out of date. The latest full run is in `/tmp/redmine_test3.log`: **6334 runs, 34686 assertions, 8 failures, 0 errors, 25 skips**.\n\nI fixed the 13 problems that came from this Mac:\n- **12 wiki ordering failures:** the macOS `en_US.UTF-8` collation sorts Cyrillic titles before Latin ones, unlike Linux in CI. I recreated the test database with `C` collation.\n- **1 Gantt PNG export error:** ImageMagick had no default font. I registered Arial in `~/.config/ImageMagick/type.xml`.\n\nThe 8 remaining failures do not come from this environment, and I did not change any code or tests for them:\n- **7 asset-link tests** (ThemesTest x3, LayoutTest x1, IssuesControllerTest x3): they check links with a regex that contains `\\w`. With the current gem versions (rails-dom-testing 2.3.0 and Nokogiri 1.19.6), the backslash gets dropped, so the check fails even though the pages render the correct links.\n- **1 CommonMark sanitization test:** the current gem versions escape `<` and `>` inside an HTML attribute, and the test expects them unescaped.\n\nBoth look like changes in newer gem versions. The repo has no committed `Gemfile.lock`, so a fresh install picks up the latest versions.\n\nRun the suite with `PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/ruby/bin:$PATH bin/rails test`. PostgreSQL 14 must stay running as a brew service for it to work."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1866,"cache_read_input_tokens":74497,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1866},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"